  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "1: Setup",
  "nextTour": "2: Configure tenant settings",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Introduction",
      "description": "## Introduction \n\nIn this lab, you will learn how to protect your MCP server by requiring access tokens from authorized clients. \n\nBy the end of this lab, you will have an MCP server that:\n\n- Requires access tokens for all incoming requests.\n\n- Validates OAuth 2.0 access tokens from authorized clients.\n\n- Enforces role-based access control to manage tool permissions."
    },
    {
      "title": "Prerequisites",
      "description": "## Prerequisites\n\nIn addition to your Auth0 account, you will need to:\n\n1. Authorize the Auth0 Labs Extension to configure your Auth0 tenant for secure tool access.\n2. Enable your tenant to use the Resource Parameter Compatibility Profile.\n\n> If you haven't completed the first prerequisite, go back to **0: Sign in** to authorize the Auth0 Labs Extension. We'll cover the second prerequisite in the next step."
    },
    {
      "title": "Enable your tenant to use the Resource Parameter Compatibility Profile",
      "description": "## Enable your tenant to use the Resource Parameter Compatibility Profile\n\nTo use the resource parameter in your access tokens, you need to enable the Resource Parameter Compatibility Profile.\n\nThe quickest way to enable it is through the Auth0 Dashboard:\n\n1. From the Auth0 Dashboard, go to **Settings** on the left menu.\n2. Select the **Advanced** tab.\n3. Scroll down to the Settings section and enable the **Resource Parameter Compatibility Profile** toggle.\n4. Select **Save**.",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 4
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 38
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Prerequisites complete!",
      "description": "## Prerequisites complete!\n\nYou are now ready to complete this lab."
    }
  ]
}